        "paragraph_id": "2B39A18F",
        "text": "In which the dimensionless sediment diameter (D*) can be calculated with the following formulation. The v is the kinematic viscosity based on the expression of Van Rijn and is a function of the water temperature. XBeach assumes a constant temperature of 20 degrees Celsius, this result in a constant kinematic viscosity of 10-6 m2/s. Note that the D50 cancels in the Asb formulation (Soulsby, 1992, eq 136b)"
      }
